      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily ibuprofen dose for adults.\n\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual ceiling is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, given as 800 mg up to four times daily. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at 6,400 mg/day:** The risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily:** 1,600 mg/day total, a common dose for mild to moderate pain.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg PO three or four times daily:** 2,400 to 3,200 mg/day, for inflammatory conditions or more severe pain.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally after checking with your resident or attending. I'll enter it once you confirm. Please also tell me the indication and whether you want a note on the order, such as \"take with food.\""
      }
     ],
